    {
      "title": "Semantically Enriching Investor Micro-blogs for Opinion-Aware Emotion Analysis: A Practical Approach",
      "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.03092",
      "description": "arXiv:2605.03092v1 Announce Type: new \nAbstract: While sentiment analysis is the staple of financial NLP, capturing the nuances of 'why' behind that sentiment remains a challenge. There have been attempts to address this by analysing investor emotions alongside sentiment; however, this does not provide the additional granularity required to understand the target of the emotion/sentiment. We address this by augmenting the StockEmotions dataset with semantically structured opinion graphs, which provide granular semantic depth to the existing sentiment and emotion labels. Using a declarative LLM pipeline, we augment the StockEmotions dataset with opinion graphs for each sentence, derived from 10,000 comments collected from StockTwits. In addition, we study the effect of introducing opinion semantics on baseline classifiers using Graph Neural Networks (GNNs). Our analysis demonstrates that incorporating opinion semantics improves classification performance across different emotional spectrums",
      "pub_date": "Wed, 06 May 2026 00:00:00 -0400",
      "source_feed": "arxiv_cs_cl",
      "_source": "rss",
      "_analysis": {
        "title": "面向投资者微博的语义增强观点感知情感分析方法",
        "summary": "针对金融情感分析中缺乏对情感目标细粒度理解的问题，本文通过为StockEmotions数据集添加语义结构化的观点图来增强情感分析。利用声明式LLM流水线，从StockTwits评论中提取观点图，并结合图神经网络（GNN）进行情感分类。实验表明，引入观点语义能提升不同情感谱系的分类性能。",
        "summary_en": "To address the lack of fine-grained understanding of sentiment targets in financial NLP, this paper augments the StockEmotions dataset with semantically structured opinion graphs. Using a declarative LLM pipeline, it extracts opinion graphs from StockTwits comments and applies GNNs for classification, showing improved performance across emotional spectrums.",
